<article class="article">
<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Pricing</span>
<h1>Honda Air Blade vs Electric Motorbike: Hanoi Rental Cost Comparison</h1>
<p>The Honda Air Blade and the electric motorbike publish identical verified rates in Hanoi: 200,000 VND per day, 1,000,000 VND per week, and a single monthly figure of 1,500,000 VND for each, confirmed at the counter as one number rather than a range. That makes this comparison unusual among rental cost guides, because the money cannot decide it. Both ladders match at every period, both share the same break-even points, and the honest difference between the two machines lives entirely off the price list: one runs on petrol bought at Hanoi stations, and the other runs on a charging routine agreed at handover. This page reads the two identical price lists side by side and then asks the questions the numbers cannot answer.</p>
<p>We compare the daily, weekly and monthly structures, the shared break-even logic, the fuel-versus-charging running line, what each machine buys as a ride, who each suits, and the deposit, gear and support questions that come with either choice. Start at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">Hanoi motorbike rental cost</a> hub, see the full model range at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> guide, and check common questions on the <a href="/faq/">rental FAQ</a>.</p>
<nav class="toc">
<ol>
<li><a href="#sec-1">The verified price ladders</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-2">Daily rate comparison</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-3">Weekly and monthly comparison</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-4">The shared break-even logic</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-5">Fuel versus charging</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-6">What each machine buys as a ride</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-7">Deposits, gear and support</a></li>
